# The request pane's edit split (http.toggle_edit_split): the primary
# tab on the left, a second tab on the right with its own strip; bringing
# the right tab to the left swaps the halves so both stay visible; the
# split is pane state and the orientation cycles with its own command.
# The strips are Rust's: every label always shows, the active one
# carries a `━` bar on the row below — so the halves are told apart by
# the `│` between them and by what each half's content says.
write anchor.txt anchor
open anchor.txt
command http.new
expect screen contains "Params  Body  Headers  Auth  Vars  Script"
expect screen lacks "Script│"
expect screen lacks "env: dev.env"
command http.toggle_edit_split
expect screen contains "edit split: Body | Vars"
# Two strips: the left one ends at the divider, the right one follows
# it; the right half is the Vars tab.
expect screen contains "Script│  Params  Body"
expect screen contains "env: dev.env"
# Ctrl+5 (Vars) on the left swaps the halves: both tabs stay on screen.
key ctrl+5
expect screen contains "Script│  Params  Body"
expect screen contains "env: dev.env"
# Off again: only the primary strip is left, and it now shows Vars.
command http.toggle_edit_split
expect screen contains "edit split: off"
expect screen lacks "Script│"
expect screen contains "env: dev.env"
command http.toggle_split_orientation
expect screen contains "request / response: vertical"
command http.toggle_split_orientation
expect screen contains "request / response: horizontal"
